helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id1106200812072645				0	eu	Text Orientation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id1106200812072653				0	eu	This feature is only available if complex text layout support is enabled in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language settings - Languages\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id1106200812112444				0	eu	Text Direction				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id1106200812112530				0	eu	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specify the text direction for a paragraph that uses complex text layout (CTL). This feature is only available if complex text layout support is enabled.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	tit				0	eu	Scale				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150868				0	eu	\<bookmark_value\>scaling; axes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>logarithmic scaling along axes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts;scaling axes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>X axes;scaling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Y axes; scaling\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150868				0	eu	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040201.xhp\" name=\"Eskala\"\>Eskala\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	eu	Y ardatzaren eskala kontrolatzen du. X-Y diagrametan, X ardatza ere eskalan jar daiteke hemen.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	eu	Y ardatza automatikoki jartzen du eskalan $[officename](e)k; horrela, balio guztiak modu optimoan erakusten dira.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	eu	Emaitza jakin bat lortu nahi baduzu, eskuz alda dezakezu ardatzaren eskala. Esate baterako, zutabeen goiko zatiak soilik bistara ditzakezu zero marra gorantz lerratuz.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154730				0	eu	Scale				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	eu	You can enter values for subdividing axes in this area. You can automatically set the properties \<emph\>Minimum, Maximum, Major interval, Minor interval count\</emph\> and \<emph\>Reference value\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150751				0	eu	Minimoa				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153713				0	eu	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_EDT_MIN\"\>Defines the minimum value for the beginning of the axis.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156385				0	eu	Maximoa				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159266				0	eu	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_EDT_MAX\"\>Defines the maximum value for the end of the axis.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155336				0	eu	Major interval				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3143218				0	eu	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_EDT_STEP_MAIN\"\>Defines the interval for the main division of the axes.\</ahelp\> The main interval cannot be larger than the value area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154020				0	eu	Minor interval count				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	eu	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_EDT_STEP_HELP\"\>Defines the interval for the subdivision of the axes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150089				0	eu	Reference value				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	eu	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_EDT_ORIGIN\"\>Specifies at which position to display the values along the axis.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166432				0	eu	Automatikoa				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145389				0	eu	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE:CBX_AUTO_ORIGIN\"\>You must first deselect the \<emph\>Automatic\</emph\> option in order to modify the values.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149129				0	eu	Balio "finkoak" erabiltzen ari bazara, desgaitu eginbide hau, ez baitu onartzen eskala automatikorik.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159206				0	eu	Eskala logaritmikoa				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145360				0	eu	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE:CBX_LOGARITHM\"\>Specifies that you want the axis to be subdivided logarithmically.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153956				0	eu	Erabili eginbide hau, elkarren artean oso desberdinak diren balioak erabiltzen ari bazara. Eskala logaritmikoa erabil dezakezu, halaber, sareta-marrak ardatzarekiko distantziakideak izan daitezen, baina handitu eta txikitu daitezkeen balioekin.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id9941404				0	eu	Reverse direction				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id5581835				0	eu	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Defines where the lower and where the higher values are displayed at the axis. The unchecked state is the mathematical direction.\</ahelp\> That means for Cartesian coordinate systems that the x-axis shows the lower values on the left and the y-axis shows the lower values at the bottom. For polar coordinate systems the mathematical angle axis direction is counterclockwise and the radial axis is from inner to outer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id922204				0	eu	Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id59225				0	eu	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For some types of axes, you can select to format an axis as text or date, or to detect the type automatically.\</ahelp\> For the axis type "Date" you can set the following options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id1159225				0	eu	Minimum and maximum value to be shown on the ends of the scale.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id2259225				0	eu	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Resolution can be set to show days, months, or years as interval steps.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3359225				0	eu	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Major interval can be set to show a certain number of days, months, or years.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id4459225				0	eu	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Minor interval can be set to show a certain number of days, months, or years.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
