helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164897K				0	eu	\<bookmark_value\>COUNTIFS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>counting;specified cells\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164897K				0	eu	COUNTIFS				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164926K				0	eu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZAEHLENWNRNG\"\>Count the number of cells that meet multiple criteria in multiple ranges.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164953K				0	eu	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164967K				0	eu	COUNTIFS( Reference R1 ; Criterion C1 [ ; Reference R2 ; Criterion C2 ]... )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164980K				0	eu	\<emph\>Reference R1\</emph\> is the  range to which the \<emph\>Criterion C1\</emph\>applies. \<emph\>Reference R2\</emph\> is the  range to which the \<emph\>Criterion C2\</emph\>applies, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165000K				0	eu	All \<emph\>Reference \</emph\> ranges shall have the same dimension and size, else an Error is returned. \<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> indicates the criteria in the form of a number, an expression or a character string. These criteria determine which cells are counted. You may also enter a search text in the form of a regular expression, e.g. b.* for all words that begin with b. You may also indicate a cell range that contains the search criterion. If you search for literal text, enclose the text in double quotes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165037K				0	eu	Examples:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3166505K				0	eu	A1:A10 is a cell range containing the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2000\</item\> to \<item type=\"input\"\>2009\</item\>. B1:B10 is a cell range containing the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2007\</item\> to \<item type=\"input\"\>2016\</item\>:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3581652K				0	eu	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIFS(A1:A10;2006;B1:B10;2014)\</item\> - this returns 2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5169225K				0	eu	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIFS(A1:A10;">=2006";B1:B10;">=2006") \</item\>- this returns 14				20200411 15:09:53
